              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to declare, then the Russian for to be considered."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: аргумент",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "аргумент (argumént) — \"an argument (a reason)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Это сильный аргумент. Éto sílnyy argumént. That is a strong argument."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. A reason in a debate, not a quarrel: a quarrel is спор or ссора."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "аргумент (argumént) is usually traced, through German and Polish, to Latin argūmentum \"proof, evidence\" (Lewis & Short), built on arguere \"to make clear, to prove\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
