        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: довод",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "довод (dóvod) — \"a point made, a reason given\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Его доводы меня не убедили. Yegó dóvody menyá ne ubedíli. His points did not convince me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. More bookish than аргумент (argumént): привести довод (dóvod) — to put forward a point."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "довод (dóvod) is built from до- \"up to\" and вод-, the root of водить \"to lead\", the iterative partner of вести, from Proto-Slavic voditi \"to lead, to conduct\" (EtymDB). A point made leads the listener up to a conclusion."
            }
          ]
        },
