          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "доказывать (dokázyvat) — \"to prove\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Он долго доказывал, что прав. On dólgo dokázyval, chto prav. He spent a long time proving that he was right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective, with the perfective доказать (докажу, докажешь). Доказывать, что… — to prove that…"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "доказывать (dokázyvat) is built from до- and казать \"to show\", the verb inside показывать and сказать. Казать is inherited from Proto-Slavic kazati (EtymDB): to prove is to show a thing through to the end."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
