          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "убедительный (ubedítelnyy) — \"convincing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Его ответ был не очень убедительным. Yegó otvét byl ne óchen ubedítelnym. His answer was not very convincing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From убедить, to convince. Убедительная просьба — an urgent request, a fixed formula on notices."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "убедительный (ubedítelnyy) is built on убедить \"to convince\". The root is that of беда \"trouble\", inherited from Proto-Slavic běda, which EtymDB sets beside Greek peíthō \"I persuade\" (EtymDB). To convince someone was first to press them hard."
            }
          ]
        },
